import json, re
V = [
("rudi at the laundromat", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone in the laundromat and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with humming washing machines, a dryer drum turning, a magazine page flipping and a fluorescent light buzzing. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Charmander never speaks human words, it only makes small "glu" sounds and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only people who speak are @Jonas and the woman with the laundry basket, and each turns their face to the camera before speaking so their lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A small laundromat with a row of washing machines and detergent bottles. @Jonas in his red backwards cap and green hoodie sits on top of a washing machine reading a magazine. In the open dryer drum in the foreground, his small orange Charmander sits in warm laundry with a grey sock in its mouth, a black scorched hole in the sock, its tail flame lighting the drum. A woman with a laundry basket stands in the doorway staring. For the first two seconds the Charmander just chews the sock and Jonas turns a page. Then the woman looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with her lips moving: "Das ist meine Wäsche. Das ist mein Trockner." Jonas doesn't look up. The Charmander pulls the sock out of its mouth, looks at the hole, and puts it back in. Jonas turns another page, then looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with his lips moving: "Er mag es warm. Der Trockner war eh an." The woman says, lips moving: "Der war nicht an. Der brennt." Thin smoke starts curling out of the drum. Jonas closes the magazine, looks at the smoke, looks at the camera, and says: "Rudi. Raus." The Charmander climbs out with the sock and sits on the floor, its tail flame flickering. Jonas opens the magazine again. The woman puts down her basket and takes out her phone. Cold white fluorescent light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("bo made a friend", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone in the car park and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with wind, cars passing, crinkling paper and two small animals chewing loudly. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Pikachu and the Rattata never speak human words, they only make small "pika" and squeaking sounds and their mouths never move to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Nele, and she turns her face to the camera so her lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A fast-food car park with a red bench. @Nele in her denim jacket holds up an empty paper bag with a pouting, betrayed face, while on the bench the yellow Pikachu and a small purple Rattata sit side by side over a pile of chips, both chewing with their cheeks full. For the first two seconds Nele just holds the bag up and the two of them chew. Then Nele looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with her lips moving: "Ich hab die Tüte zwei Sekunden hingelegt. Zwei." The Rattata grabs three chips at once and stuffs them in its mouth, the Pikachu looks at it, then does the same. Nele says, lips moving: "Und jetzt hat er einen Freund. Toll. Zwei Diebe." The Rattata pushes a single chip toward the Pikachu with its nose. The Pikachu eats it. Nele looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Nein, wir nehmen die Ratte nicht mit." The Rattata looks up at her with its mouth full. Nele closes her eyes, sighs, and sits down on the bench next to them. The Pikachu offers her a chip. Grey overcast light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("herbert on the escalator", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone at the bottom of the escalator and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with the hum of an escalator, mall music, footsteps and shoppers talking. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Psyduck never speaks human words, it only makes a small panicked "psy" sound and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Lukas, and when he speaks he turns his face to the camera so his lips are visible moving. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A shopping mall escalator with shoppers on the steps above. @Lukas in his grey hoodie with the hood up sleeps standing on a step, leaning sideways against the handrail, and two steps above him the yellow Psyduck stands with both hands on its head, staring down at the camera in panic. For the first two seconds the escalator carries them slowly upward and nothing else moves. Then the Psyduck's eyes go wider, it looks at the top of the escalator, then back at the camera, and lets out a small "psy". Lukas's hand slides along the handrail as the steps move, his body tilting further. The Psyduck reaches down and tugs at his hood with one hand, still holding its head with the other. Lukas opens one eye, turns his face to the camera, listens for two seconds, and mumbles with his lips moving: "Sind wir oben?" He closes the eye again. The Psyduck tugs harder. Lukas says, eyes closed, lips moving: "Herbert. Nicht jetzt." A woman with shopping bags steps around them shaking her head. The top of the escalator comes closer, the Psyduck grabs Lukas's hood with both hands and braces its feet. Cold white mall light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("mira got a fan", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone while walking backwards ahead of her and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that swings with every step, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with footsteps on tarmac, wind in hedges and small soft padding steps. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Jigglypuff never speaks human words, it only says a happy "puff" and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Mira, and she looks at the camera so her lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A quiet suburban street with tall hedges, two friends blurred at the left and right edges. @Mira in her red beanie and navy rain jacket walks toward the camera with her hands in her pockets and a dead-eyed face, and next to her the round pink Jigglypuff waddles along wearing an identical tiny red beanie, looking up at her adoringly. For the first two seconds Mira just walks, not looking down. The Jigglypuff has to take three quick steps for every one of hers. Mira looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says flatly, lips moving: "Ich hab ihm die Mütze nicht gegeben. Es hatte sie einfach." The Jigglypuff says a proud "puff" and adjusts the beanie with one tiny hand. Mira stops walking. The Jigglypuff stops. Mira walks on. The Jigglypuff walks on. Mira looks at the camera again, waits two seconds, and says: "Nein. Es hat keinen Namen. Es heißt nicht Pummel." The Jigglypuff hears the word, spins around once with joy, and bumps into her leg. Mira closes her eyes for a moment and keeps walking. Grey overcast light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("sam's new rod", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone on the wet pier and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with rain on jackets, water under the pier, a pelican croaking and a fish flapping. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The only people who speak are @Sam and @Mira, and each turns their face to the camera before speaking so their lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A wooden pier on a grey lake in the rain, hooded people fishing in the background, a pelican on a post. @Sam in his black rain jacket with the hood up holds up a brand new fishing rod with the price tag still dangling, grinning, an orange Magikarp hanging from the line. Next to him @Mira in her red beanie and grey hoodie holds a coffee cup and stares at the fish with a blank face. For the first two seconds the fish just hangs there dripping and Sam grins. Then Sam looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with his lips moving: "Neue Rute, erster Wurf, zack. Das ist Talent." Mira says, lips moving, without looking away from the fish: "Das ist derselbe Fisch wie letzte Woche." Sam says: "Das ist ein anderer." The Magikarp flaps once, hard, and the pelican on the post opens its beak and leans toward it. Mira looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Er hat noch nicht mal das Preisschild ab." Sam looks at the tag, rips it off with his teeth, and holds the rod higher. The pelican takes off from the post. Sam sees it coming, turns, and the camera follows as he runs down the pier with the fish swinging and the pelican after him. Mira takes a sip of coffee. Grey rainy light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("yuna vs the vending machine", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone in the bus shelter and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with a humming vending machine, a jet of water hitting glass, traffic and teenagers talking behind. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Squirtle never speaks human words, it only makes small "squirt" sounds and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Yuna, and she turns her face to the camera so her lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A bus shelter at dusk with a glowing snack vending machine, three boys in hoodies watching in the background. @Yuna in her yellow raincoat points at the machine with an angry battle face, while her small blue Squirtle sprays a jet of water into the coin slot, water running down the glass, a bag of crisps stuck halfway inside. For the first two seconds the Squirtle keeps spraying and the machine hums. Then the crisps don't move. Yuna turns to the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with her lips moving: "Der hat mein Geld genommen. Jetzt kriegt er das." She points again: "Aquaknarre. Nochmal." The Squirtle takes a deep breath and sprays harder, the whole front of the machine streams with water, the lights inside flicker. One of the boys behind says something to the other and both laugh. Yuna looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Nein, ich rüttel nicht. Rütteln ist verboten. Das hier nicht." The machine sparks once, goes dark, and the crisps drop with a thud. The Squirtle stops spraying and looks at Yuna. Yuna picks up the crisps, opens the packet, and says: "Sieg." Cold blue dusk light, glowing machine. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("the snorlax moved", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone at the edge of the crater and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with wind in wet trees, dripping leaves, birds and a distant tractor. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The only people who speak are @Jonas and @Lukas, and each turns his face to the camera before speaking so his lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A misty country road between trees and a wooden fence. In the tarmac, a huge round crater with a collapsed tent and a washing line full of socks and shirts lying in it. @Jonas in his red backwards cap stands at the far edge with his hands on his hips, @Lukas in his grey hoodie next to him holding one grey sock. For the first two seconds both just stare into the crater. Then Jonas looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with his lips moving: "Fünf Tage. Fünf Tage haben wir gewartet, und es geht, während wir Brötchen holen." Lukas holds up the sock and says, lips moving: "Das ist meine einzige. Die andere ist da drin geblieben." He points at the crater. Jonas crouches, picks up a flattened tent pole, looks at it, drops it. He looks at the camera again, waits two seconds, and says: "Nein, wir suchen es nicht. Es ist ein Relaxo. Es liegt irgendwo." A deep distant thud echoes through the mist from somewhere down the road. Both turn their heads toward it. Lukas says, lips moving: "Da." Jonas says: "Da." Neither moves. Misty grey light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("group photo attempt 7", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone on the hill to take a group photo and hit record by mistake. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes and swings in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with wind on the hill, shouting, a fish slapping on grass and a small flame hissing. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Charmander, the Pikachu and the Magikarp never speak human words, they only make "glu", "pika" and wet flapping sounds and their mouths never move to any sentence. The only people who speak are @Jonas, @Nele and @Sam, and each turns their face to the camera before speaking so their lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A grassy hilltop with a town far below, overcast sky. @Jonas in his green hoodie and red backwards cap shouts with his mouth open while the small orange Charmander on his shoulder has set the sleeve of @Sam, black jacket at the left edge, smoking. @Nele in her denim jacket screams with the yellow Pikachu sitting on her head holding a sandwich, and an orange Magikarp flops on the grass in the foreground. For the first two seconds everyone is frozen mid-shout as if waiting for me to count. Then Sam slaps his smoking sleeve with his other hand and shouts, lips moving: "Rudi! Nicht schon wieder!" Jonas grabs the Charmander off his shoulder and says, lips moving: "Er hat sich nur gefreut." The Pikachu drops the sandwich onto Nele's face, she pulls it off and says, lips moving: "Bo. Runter. Jetzt." The Magikarp flops straight at the camera and the picture jerks sideways. Nele looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says: "Noch einmal. Ein einziges Mal. Alle gucken." All three straighten up, the Charmander on Jonas's shoulder, the Pikachu on Nele's head, the Magikarp still flopping. They hold a smile for one second, then the sleeve starts smoking again. Grey overcast light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("rain day", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone under the bus shelter and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with heavy rain drumming on the shelter roof, cars hissing past on wet tarmac, a small hissing flame and dripping water. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Charmander and the Pikachu never speak human words, they only make small "glu" and "pika" sounds and their mouths never move to any sentence. The only people who speak are @Mira, @Nele and @Jonas, and each turns their face to the camera before speaking so their lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A bus stop in pouring rain at dusk, street lights blurred behind. @Mira in her red beanie, @Nele in her denim jacket holding the umbrella with the Pikachu's face peeking out of her jacket, and @Jonas in his green hoodie and red backwards cap squeeze under one small umbrella, all soaked, while the small orange Charmander stands at their feet with a plastic bucket over its head and its tail flame steaming in the rain. For the first two seconds they all just stare down the road, water dripping off them. Then Jonas turns to the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with his lips moving: "Der Bus kommt. Der kommt immer." Mira says, lips moving, without turning: "Vor vierzig Minuten hast du das auch gesagt." A car drives through a puddle and sprays all three of them. Nobody reacts. The Charmander's flame flickers and hisses under the rain, the Pikachu pulls its head back inside Nele's jacket. Nele looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Nein, wir laufen nicht. Rudi geht im Regen aus." Jonas says: "Rudi geht nicht aus. Rudi ist nur sauer." The Charmander tips the bucket further over its eyes. Mira looks at the camera and says: "Ich bin auch sauer." Cold grey-blue rain light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("bo's first battle", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I crouched down on the path with my old iPhone and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with wind in tall grass, footsteps on dry earth and birds. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Pikachu and the Caterpie never speak human words, they only make small "pika" and tiny chirping sounds and their mouths never move to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Nele, and she turns her face to the camera before speaking so her lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A dirt path through tall grass under a grey sky, two friends walking up behind, out of focus. @Nele in her denim jacket and cap points forward with a stern face, while her yellow Pikachu hides behind her leg peeking around her knee with big scared eyes. In the foreground on the path, a tiny green Caterpie sits looking at them. For the first two seconds nothing moves except the Caterpie slowly lifting its head. Then Nele says, lips moving, pointing: "Bo. Los. Das ist eine Raupe." The Pikachu presses itself tighter against her leg and shakes its head. The Caterpie inches one centimetre forward. The Pikachu squeaks and climbs halfway up Nele's leg. Nele turns to the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with her lips moving: "Nein, ich helf ihm nicht. Er muss das lernen." She peels the Pikachu off her leg and sets it down on the path facing the Caterpie. The two stare at each other. The Caterpie chirps. The Pikachu turns around and runs straight back behind Nele's leg. Nele looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Erster Kampf. Verloren gegen eine Raupe." The Caterpie slowly crawls off the path into the grass. Grey overcast light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("he adopted it", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone by the park bench and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with wind in bare trees, ducks on the pond, gravel crunching and a slow snore. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Slowpoke and the Psyduck never speak human words, they only make small "slow" and "psy" sounds and their mouths never move to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Lukas, and he turns his face to the camera so his lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A park bench by a grey pond with bare trees. @Lukas in his grey hoodie with the hood up lies on the bench half asleep, and on the bench in front of him a fat pink Slowpoke lies with its mouth hanging open and a blank happy face. On the gravel next to the bench, the yellow Psyduck stands with its arms crossed glaring at the Slowpoke. For the first two seconds nothing moves except the Slowpoke slowly blinking. Then the Psyduck stamps one foot on the gravel with an angry "psy". Lukas opens his eyes, looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with his lips moving: "Der lag einfach da. Ich hab nichts gemacht." The Slowpoke yawns very slowly and rolls half a turn toward Lukas. The Psyduck stamps again. Lukas says, lips moving: "Herbert. Ihr könnt euch das Bett teilen." The Psyduck turns its back to the bench and sits down on the gravel with its hands on its head. Lukas looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Zwei Pokémon, die nichts tun. Passt zu mir." He closes his eyes. The Slowpoke says a very slow "slooow". Grey winter light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("mira's birthday", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone across the café table and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with café chatter, cups clinking, a coffee machine hissing and a small candle flame. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Jigglypuff never speaks human words, it only says a happy "puff" and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only people who speak are @Mira and @Nele, and each turns her face to the camera before speaking so her lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A warm café with fairy lights, friends in caps standing behind, two people with their backs to me at the near end of the table. Across the table, @Mira in her red beanie and navy jacket stares straight into the camera with a dead expression behind a small chocolate cake with one lit candle, the round pink Jigglypuff sitting next to the cake with cream on its feet, and @Nele in her denim jacket next to her, frowning at the camera. For the first two seconds nobody moves and the candle flickers, as if everyone is waiting for me to finish singing. Then Nele looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with her lips moving: "Das war das Lied? Das ganze Lied?" Mira says, without changing her face, lips moving: "Reicht." The Jigglypuff puffs itself up, takes a huge breath to sing, and Mira puts one hand flat on top of its head without looking at it. It deflates with a squeak. Nele laughs. Mira leans forward, blows out the candle, and the Jigglypuff immediately sticks one foot into the cake. Mira looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Bestes Geburtstag. Ever." Nele says, lips moving: "Sie meint das ernst." Mira takes the Jigglypuff's foot out of the cake and eats the cream off it. Warm café light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("sam in the aquarium", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone in the aquarium and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: dark, soft focus, heavy visible noise and compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with the low hum of aquarium pumps, echoing footsteps and murmuring visitors. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Gyarados never speaks and makes no sound except a deep muffled rumble through the glass. The only person who speaks is @Sam, and he turns his face toward the camera so his lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A dark aquarium hall, blue light from a huge tank, visitors in the background. @Sam in his black rain jacket stands with both hands and his face pressed flat against the glass, smiling, while a gigantic blue Gyarados fills the tank behind the glass, its huge eye level with Sam's face. For the first two seconds nothing moves but the Gyarados slowly blinking. Then the Gyarados opens its mouth wide, showing its teeth, and Sam doesn't flinch at all. Sam turns his head to the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with his lips moving: "Der mag mich. Guck doch. Der mag mich." The Gyarados slams its head against the glass with a deep thud, the whole tank shudders, visitors behind jump back. Sam presses his face back to the glass and says, lips moving: "Das war ein Kuss." The Gyarados's eye narrows and it slowly sinks out of view into the dark water. Sam looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Ich hol die Angel." Cold blue aquarium light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("yuna's shopping list", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone in the shop queue and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with a beeping till, shop music, glass bottles clinking and a squeaky trolley wheel. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Squirtle never speaks human words, it only makes small "squirt" sounds and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only people who speak are @Yuna and @Sam, and each turns their face to the camera before speaking so their lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. Inside a small Poké Mart with shelves of boxes and plush toys. @Yuna in her yellow raincoat stands behind a shopping trolley piled dangerously high with purple potion bottles, reading a long paper list, while her small blue Squirtle sits on top of the pile. Behind her @Sam in his black rain jacket holds one small packet of fishing bait and stares at the pile. For the first two seconds Yuna just reads, her lips moving silently as she counts, and the Squirtle wobbles on the bottles. Then Yuna looks up at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with her lips moving: "Vierzig. Das reicht für drei Kämpfe. Vielleicht vier." Sam leans in and says, lips moving: "Das ist mehr als das Regal hatte." Yuna says, lips moving: "Ich hab das Lager gefragt." The trolley squeaks, tilts, one bottle rolls off the top and Sam catches it without looking. The Squirtle slides down the pile and lands on the floor with a "squirt". Yuna looks at the camera again, waits two seconds, and says: "Nein. Ich brauch die alle." She picks up the Squirtle, puts it back on the pile, and pushes the trolley forward. Cold white shop light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("rudi's bath day", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone in the bathroom doorway and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with running water, splashing, a small hissing flame and an echoing tiled bathroom. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Charmander never speaks human words, it only makes small "glu" and hissing sounds and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Jonas, and he turns his face to the camera so his lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. A small steamy tiled bathroom with a mirror, a sink full of foam and a scorched towel on the rail. @Jonas in his red backwards cap and a grey shirt with rolled-up sleeves holds his small orange Charmander standing in the sink with both hands, the Charmander holding its flaming tail stiffly up out of the water with an outraged face and foam on its head. For the first two seconds the Charmander just stands there dripping and glaring. Jonas turns to the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with his lips moving: "Er hat auf dem Sofa geschlafen. Auf dem verbrannten Sofa. Er riecht wie ein Lagerfeuer." He scoops water over the Charmander's head, it squeezes its eyes shut and hisses, the tail flame flares and the steam gets thicker. Jonas says, lips moving: "Rudi. Flamme runter." The flame shrinks slightly. Jonas looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Nein, das Handtuch war schon so." The Charmander shakes itself like a dog, foam flies everywhere, onto Jonas's cap and onto the lens. Jonas wipes his face slowly and says: "Zweimal im Jahr. Mehr nicht." Warm steamy bathroom light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("the ferry again", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone on the ferry deck and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that sways with the boat, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with wind, engine rumble, seagulls and a low humming. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Psyduck never speaks human words, it only makes a strained "psy" sound and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Mira, and she looks at the camera so her lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. The open deck of a rusty ferry on a grey sea. In the foreground @Lukas in his grey hoodie sleeps on a bench with his head tipped back, next to him the yellow Psyduck holds its head with its eyes glowing faintly blue. Behind them @Mira in her red beanie and red hoodie stands with a coffee cup and a completely bored face while her hair floats straight up, and around her a handbag, a backpack, a seagull and a bin float in the air, a bicycle leaning against the rail starting to lift. For the first two seconds nothing happens except the objects drifting slowly higher. Mira takes a sip of coffee. Then she looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, and says flatly, lips moving: "Jedes Mal. Jede einzelne Fähre." The bicycle rises past her head. She ducks slightly without changing her expression. The seagull, floating upside down, flaps in confusion. Mira looks at the camera again, waits two seconds, and says: "Nein, ich weck ihn nicht. Dann wird es schlimmer." The Psyduck lets out a long "psyyy", everything drops at once with a crash, the bicycle clatters onto the deck, the seagull lands on the bin and squawks. Lukas doesn't wake up. Mira takes another sip. Grey sea light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("gym number 2", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone on the gym steps and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that shakes in my hand, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with wind, a flapping paper sign, distant traffic and a heavy wooden door. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Squirtle never speaks human words, it only makes small "squirt" sounds and its mouth never moves to any sentence. The only people who speak are @Yuna and @Nele, and each turns her face to the camera before speaking so her lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. The front of a big stone gym building with tall green double doors, a hand-written paper sign taped to the door. @Yuna in her yellow raincoat stands in front of the doors with her arms out in disbelief, her small blue Squirtle on the step below. Next to her @Nele in her denim jacket has her hand over her mouth trying not to laugh. For the first two seconds Yuna just stares at the sign with her arms out. Then she turns to the camera, listens for two seconds, and says with her lips moving: "Geschlossen. Wegen Wasserschaden. WASSERSCHADEN." Nele snorts and says, lips moving: "Wer hat wohl den Wasserschaden gemacht." Yuna says: "Das war ein Kampf. Das zählt nicht." The Squirtle looks up at her and blinks innocently. Yuna bangs on the door with her fist, the sign flaps. Nele looks at the camera, waits two seconds, and says: "Ja, seit einer halben Stunde." Yuna sits down on the step next to the Squirtle, arms crossed, and says, lips moving: "Ich warte. Ich hab Zeit." The Squirtle sprays a tiny jet of water at the door. Nele laughs harder. Grey overcast light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
("3 hours of this pt. 2", """Candid first-person video from my own eye level, as if I just raised my old iPhone from my seat on the bus and hit record. 2015 smartphone video quality: soft focus, visible noise and slight compression, motion blur, uneven handheld framing that rocks with the bus, people cut off at the edges, no flash, no filter, audio like a phone microphone with a rattling bus, rain on the windows, soft snoring and a crinkling packet. The person holding the camera never speaks and makes no sound. The Pikachu and the Psyduck never speak human words, they only make small "pika" and "psy" sounds and their mouths never move to any sentence. The only person who speaks is @Mira, and she looks at the camera so her lips are visible moving with every word. All dialogue is spoken in casual, natural German. The Snapchat caption bar with the white text in the photo stays exactly as it is on screen for the whole video, like a fixed overlay. Inside an old bus with worn blue seats and rain-streaked windows. @Lukas in his grey hoodie sleeps against the window with his mouth open, the yellow Psyduck asleep next to him holding its head. Behind them @Mira in her red beanie stares at the camera with a dead expression. In the front row @Nele with her blonde hair up has fallen asleep with her head tilted, and her Pikachu is quietly pulling snack packets out of her open backpack. For the first two seconds only the bus rocks and the Pikachu rustles. Then the Pikachu freezes with a packet in its paws and looks straight at the camera. Mira looks at the camera, listens for two seconds, then says flatly, lips moving: "Lass ihn. Ist ihr Rucksack." The Pikachu slowly, carefully, stuffs the packet into its cheek and reaches for the next one. The bus hits a bump, Lukas's head knocks against the window, he snores louder, and the Psyduck lets out a small "psy" in its sleep. Mira looks at the camera again, waits two seconds, and says: "Noch zwei Stunden. Weck mich, wenn wir da sind." She closes her eyes. The Pikachu takes a third packet. Flat grey light. Vertical 9:16. No watermark, no visible phone or camera."""),
]
